   "**Nineteen Arab-led seats have become the hinge of a government that promised not to use them** — an unprecedented turnout producing an unprecedented bloc, and all but one Jewish party pledged against partnership; the direct effect is that the largest single addition to the Knesset cannot be spent inside the coalition; the compound consequence is that support must be given from outside by parties the government has ruled out, so the government's majority is borrowed against a promise it intends to keep — and a majority that is borrowed is called in at the first security vote",
