  "verse": "Therefore it is not the truth that you can nurture thoughts and feelings at a whim, without you having to give (make) an account for it, therefore you should consider everything if villainous thoughts and feelings proceed from you, such as in relation to killing (murder), adultery, sexual decadence (sexual culpability), robbery and thieving (theft), waging battles (waging war), giving false testimony, sacrilege and slander (calumny), hatred, jealousy, revenge and retaliation as well as stinginess and many other things of a wrong sense and negative value.",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 19, Verse 20",
  "hinge": "The cause is not the weapon and not the ideology in the abstract; it is the cultivation — §19:20 says thoughts and feelings may not be nurtured \"at a whim\" and that an account must be given for them, which places the causal chain in the weeks before the square, not in the three minutes inside it. That is also where the intervention is cheapest. The change available is administrative: a single file, held by a named officer, wherever a firearm licence, a domestic-violence complaint and extremist material co-occur — and a protocol that treats a family killing as a possible prelude rather than a concluded tragedy. Kraków's police proved on Saturday that three minutes can stop a massacre. The question the country now has to answer is why the two hours before it, and the two hundred kilometres, were nobody's assignment."
